# (#126) `report of` ON A PARAMETER. Part 2a seeds an observed function's
# NUMERIC parameters into the global env at entry (aot_set) so the body's
# named reads find them; that seed -- and the #123 shadow refusal that is
# gated on the seed's own condition -- are now per-parameter. `v` is named,
# so it is seeded and observed; `s` and `n` are not, so they stay C doubles
# and the entry prologue carries no aot_set for them.
define probe(v) as:
    local s is 0.0
    local n is 0
    loop while n < 5:
        s is s + v
        v is v * 0.5
        n is n + 1
    return [report of v, s, n]
print of (probe of 10.0)
print of (probe of 4.0)
print of (probe of 1.0)
